 "provenance": "Bavaria 4 (w1 l3) secret exit 2,10, control-only on the exact S700 core. Start: lives 12 (campaign-style value used by earlier routes), weaponTier 2 (hook obtained in Bavaria 3), maxHealth 4, 0 diamonds. Route: the first 480 ticks replay the intent of the old port attempt bavaria-04-first-stone-wall: checkpoint 3,6; walking through the grass at 7,5-7,7 lets stone 8,5 roll down to 7,7, then five hook pulls (from 6,5, 7,5 and 8,5) draw stones 9,5 and 10,5 west until they drop out of row 5, clearing row 5 of the stone block at 8-10,5-7; along row 5 to 13,5 and via 13,7 and 15,7 up to 15,6. Hook pull of stone 17,9 from 15,9 into 16,9 (column 17 drops one cell, which by itself clears 17,6), then three pushes move stone 16,6 to 19,6, where it falls into 19,7 and row 6 is clear. The three red snakes on row 7 (25,7, 26,7, 27,7) are killed with three hammer hits each, about 60 ticks apart. Upper loop up column 28, along row 2, down column 34 and via 32,5-32,7 and 30,7 to checkpoint 30,10. Hook from 26,10 pulls stone 24,10 into 25,10; it falls down column 25 and crushes the three snakes at 25,13, 25,14 and 25,15. Down column 25 and along row 16; the demo dialogue at 20,16 is advanced with action presses; checkpoint 19,16. Hammer from 13,16 on brick 13,15 breaks the brick row 11-18,15, so roller 13,14 drops first and ends in pocket 14,19, and roller 17,14 then rolls left along row 18 and destroys crusher 10,17-18. Timed waits at 9,18 and 6,18 before passing the spike traps at 8,16, 7,17, 5,20 and 4,19 along row 18. Up column 2 to 2,13, then 3,13 up column 3 to 3,10 and left onto the secret exit 2,10. No damage taken, no deaths.",
